# The SuperDrastic release install.sh installs (https://github.com/JorreFog/SuperDrastic): version and the sha256 of
# superdrastic-<version>-aarch64.tar.gz. Bump both together. This release ships the package in dsflip/.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.7 is SuperDrastic v0.5.0-beta.1 (the in-game menu) plus
# dsflip/superdrastic-0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.7.patch (SuperDrastic branch claude/1-6-prep-work-kwq9lc and two commits
# made on an RG DS Plus, local branch 1.6-freeze-fix): 1.5.13's four
# commits (shader output sizes with ds-fsr at 3x on the RG DS Plus; the Wi-Fi / Nintendo WFC path; its pre-device
# fixes; the microphone's tunables, logs and joystick-button fallback) and 1.6's (the stall watch and a quit that works
# on a stuck game; new threads on every CPU; RetroAchievements logins that survive no network; online play only with
# DSFLIP_WFC; the menu's Blow on the fake microphone's real binding; DSFLIP_STALL_TEST; the in-game menu's pixel
# text on the font's grid at 640x480; DraStic's helper threads held until their locks exist, which was the freeze at
# a game's start). The same package on the RG DS and the RG DS Plus.
# Built with build.sh (clang 23 + lld, an Ubuntu noble arm64 sysroot: libc6 2.39, libdrm 2.4.125) and
# package.sh; it needs glibc 2.38 like the release. Once the patch is in a SuperDrastic release, pin that release here
# instead and drop the patch.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.1 (a PRIVATE test build, 2026-10-09; not a release): the RG DS line's .8 (the
# in-game menu's fixes and 3x's lines, SuperDrastic branch claude/open-issues-rocknix-nightly-1l4s4w) plus the 3x
# work, built from SuperDrastic's local branch opt/3x-a55-noil: the cache work of 2026-10-05 (prefetch in the pixel
# kernels, direct rendering into the scanout buffers, no copy of an unchanged 3D frame, audio without SDL's subsystem,
# test aids), SuperDrastic PR #8 (the rasterizer scheduled for the Cortex-A55; it also fixes 3x textures drawn askew)
# and #6 (3x keeps its own clock memory). Verified on this handheld: frames identical with and without PR #8 at 2x (six
# games), at 3x except where it now matches DraStic's own picture; 54 starts at 3x through this line's session.sh with
# the build before PR #8 without a freeze, and the final library in real sessions. Source: SuperDrastic's
# refs/testers/sd-9-test.1.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.4 (PRIVATE test build 4, 2026-10-11; not a release): test build 3's library merged
# into the Gengis Engine at SuperDrastic e646968 (2D scanline routines, geometry stage and A55-scheduled kernels
# replaced) with test build 3's cache work ported onto it (kernel and downsample prefetch, no copy of an unchanged
# 3D frame, direct rendering into the scanout buffers), 3x honouring disable_edge_marking, and issue 47's neighbour
# polygons at 3x. Measured on the RG DS Plus against test build 3: 3x faster in all four games tried (stress ROM
# 35.7 vs 34.9 fps at 1416 MHz, CPU a frame MKDS -4%, HeartGold -10%), 2x level; 2x exact (RAST=diff). Source:
# SuperDrastic's refs/testers/sd-9-test.4.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.9-test.6 (PRIVATE test build 6, 2026-10-11; not a release): test build 4's library with the
# CPU governor holding the power profile's bound from the start, and going past it (and remembering a clock as too
# slow) only when the game is CPU-bound. Test build 4 ran at 1992 MHz whatever the profile on the RG DS Plus. Source:
# SuperDrastic's refs/testers/sd-9-test.6.
# Released unchanged in ROCKNIXDS 1.6.2 (2026-10-12): the same package test build 7 shipped, its name kept; the
# source is tagged rocknixds-1.6.2 in SuperDrastic (783d86f).
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.10 (ROCKNIXDS 1.6.4 for the RG DS Plus, a hotfix): .9-test.6 plus the audio crackle fix,
# SuperDrastic branch plus-audio-hotfix (d8f4105 on 783d86f). DraStic's sound ran out in heavy games (Mario Kart DS
# racing: 18-33 gaps a minute, filled with zeros by DraStic's callback) when the full frame queue held it 20 ms and when
# the CPU governor tried 1104 MHz again; the hold now lets DraStic go while its sound still covers its next frame, and
# a step down that runs the sound out or drops a frame is undone for the session. Built with build.sh on a Debian trixie arm64
# sysroot (needs glibc 2.38, like .9-test.6) and package.sh.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.11 (ROCKNIXDS 1.6.4.3-plus, the agiacalone fork, 2026-11-01): .10 (d8f4105) plus fixes
# cherry-picked from the BananaOS line of SuperDrastic (git cherry-pick -x; the BananaOS line is upstream's
# 68eae50, which split from ours at 930c4c5): DraStic's clock with a gap over a second taken out (the long white
# screen after a sleep, BananaLinux #64), 21 more shaders (libretro, Anbernic, NNDDSS), ds-grid-2x 13% cheaper and
# ds-grid even on the RG DS, an opt-in display-locked sound rate (DSFLIP_AUDIO_LOCK_PER), save/load state pop-ups,
# a charger shown as charging (#35), and a TERM that stops DraStic without SuperDrastic too. One fork fix on top:
# libretro's "#pragma parameter" lines are commented out before compiling, because ROCKNIX's Mali driver refuses
# their quotes (7 of the 21 shaders failed without it). Source: dsflip/superdrastic-0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.11.patch
# (git format-patch d8f4105..b9826c4, 11 commits). Built with build.sh and package.sh in a Debian trixie container:
# clang/lld 22.1.8 (apt.llvm.org) with -fstack-protector-strong through a target config file, as Ubuntu's clang
# does by default; a rebuild of .10 there matches the shipped .10 except the compiler's name strings. Checked on an
# RG DS Plus: tools/smoke.sh (Mario Kart DS, HeartGold: 60.0 presents/s, 0 dropped, 0 underruns), all 29 shaders
# through tools/shtest at 1x and 2x, and a 5 s SIGSTOP logged and taken out by the clock fix.
# 0.5.0-beta.1-rocknixds.12 (ROCKNIXDS 1.6.4.4-plus, 2026-11-01): .11 plus phase 2 from the BananaOS line, by hand
# where the lines differ (agiacalone/SuperDrastic branch rocknixds-12; source: dsflip/superdrastic-0.5.0-beta.1-
# rocknixds.12.patch, git format-patch rocknixds-11..rocknixds-12). On by default: a quit (SIGTERM) while the in-game
# menu is open closes it and reaches DraStic; Quit without saving (X on the quit question, or its touch button).
# Off unless set, so ROCKNIX's pacing and sound stay as in .11: low latency (DSFLIP_LOWLAT=1, _QUEUE, _ALIGN), the
# sleeping sound wait (DSFLIP_AUDIO_WAIT=1), the cpugov spike rule (DSFLIP_CPUGOV_SPIKE=1), a menu clock
# (DSFLIP_CPUGOV_MENU=<kHz>), the audio hand-off at quit (DSFLIP_AUDIO_CLOSE_CHILD=1; on ROCKNIX "default" is
# PipeWire), DSFLIP_RESUME_ON_QUIT=0 (resume state on SIGUSR1 only) and DSFLIP_LOG_TIME=1. Not taken: brightness on
# the menu, the Hotkeys page and F+SELECT swap (they need BananaOS's backlight, lid and F-key code), the menu's
# translations (lang.c), and two that our line already has (slot pictures by fopen, both-screen state pictures).
# Checked on an RG DS Plus: tools/smoke.sh with defaults on HeartGold (0 dropped) and Mario Kart DS six runs
# alternating with .11 (0/6/2 dropped per 30 s against .11's 2/8/0); DSFLIP_LOWLAT=1 20 dropped per 30 s (rougher on
# the Plus, as BananaOS notes; off by default); DSFLIP_AUDIO_WAIT=1 2 dropped, 0 underruns; a SIGTERM with the menu
# open logged "quit asked while open" and the menu was back in 1 s.
# The RG DS line (ROCKNIXDS 1.6.3.2, a beta) moves from .9-test.6 to .12 in one step: the same package as the Plus's
# 1.6.4.4-plus, byte for byte. libdsflip finds the panels' size itself, and .10 to .12 changed no ROCKNIXDS script.
# Not yet checked on an RG DS: every test above ran on an RG DS Plus.
